From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 20:13:59 +0200
Subject: media: gc2145: Let the automatic exposure act on every frame

P1:0x0b[6:4] is how many frames the AEC waits between corrections, and
it comes up as 2. Both vendor drivers write 1 there. The driver was
writing nothing, so the loop ran at half the rate the sensor is capable
of - measured on a phone, the register was still at its reset value.

The rest of the loop is left alone deliberately: the slow and fast
margins and step sizes at P1:0x18/0x19 and the 1.17x gain change
deadband at P1:0x1a are all at their reset values in both vendor
drivers too, and they are the parameters that trade convergence speed
for hunting, which is not something to change without being able to
watch the result.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c | 17 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c b/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
@@ -267,6 +267,8 @@
 #define GC2145_P2_EDGE_EFFECT		0x297
 
 /* AEC, page 1 */
+#define GC2145_P1_AEC_MODE2		0x10b
+#define GC2145_AEC_MODE2_EVERY_N_FRAMES		GENMASK(6, 4)
 #define GC2145_P1_AEC_MODE3		0x10c
 #define GC2145_AEC_MODE3_CENTRE_WEIGHT		GENMASK(6, 4)
 #define GC2145_P1_AEC_ANTI_FLICKER_HI	0x125
@@ -2229,10 +2231,17 @@ static int gc2145_setup_aec(struct gc2145_dev *sensor,
 	gc2145_tx_write8(sensor, 0x107, cy1 / GC2145_AEC_WIN_RATIO);
 	gc2145_tx_write8(sensor, 0x108, cy2 / GC2145_AEC_WIN_RATIO);
 
-	// increase maximum exposure level to 4
-	//gc2145_tx_write8(sensor, 0x13c, 0x60);
-	// setup AEC mode: measure point, adjust_max_gain, skip_mode = 2
-	//gc2145_tx_write8(sensor, 0x10a, 0xc2);
+	/*
+	 * Act on every frame rather than every second one, which is what
+	 * the register comes up as. Both vendor drivers do this, and it is
+	 * the whole of the difference between them and the reset state as
+	 * far as the loop rate goes - the margins and step sizes at
+	 * P1:0x18/0x19 and the 1.17x deadband at P1:0x1a are left alone by
+	 * everyone, so they are left alone here too.
+	 */
+	gc2145_tx_update_bits(sensor, GC2145_P1_AEC_MODE2,
+			      GC2145_AEC_MODE2_EVERY_N_FRAMES,
+			      FIELD_PREP(GC2145_AEC_MODE2_EVERY_N_FRAMES, 1));
 
 	// AEC_ASDE_select_luma_value AEC_low_light_exp_THD_max:
 	//gc2145_tx_write8(sensor, 0x121, 0x15);
